      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have been wanting this feature for a long time, but it has not yet been implemented, so I am voting for it.\n\nI have a concept for an AnimatorController used in the Base of PlayabeLayers that allows the function to be deactivated by a parameter and a temporary posture control system can be attached and removed by ModularAvatar. This is actually achieved with the assets HoverMotion, RealSkateBoardMotion, and StandardMotion.\n\nThis is because Gesture does not work with Action.\n\nIn addition, we want to make sure that the original locomotion and the functionality added by ModularAvatar are smoothly animated together.\n\nThe simplest way to achieve this is to use weights to manage layers in the AnimatorController for Base.\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-24T18:17:40.012Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The Animator Layer Control state behavior currently only allows controlling the weight of layers inside Additive, FX, Gesture and Action. There are use cases where being able to control the weight of locomotion layers would be helpful.\nFor example, a transforming avatar that has multiple movement sets might be most easily done with a second animator layer in locomotion that is weighted in when in use, and back out when not. The alternative is a substatemachine with a lot of transitions leading in and out, which would be much harder to work with.",
